\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cdad9d301bec16fe086ffc0fa362cd9c209ad757a392ea99491e72fd0e6abe62","event_uuid":"73caacc1-2e33-4032-ae07-af13b4417068","position":{"commit_sha":"8e0c0245fc0b872a67fe4f9ecd6b9478afb8fcd1","position":"1785375590079297001-73caacc1-2e33-4032-ae07-af13b4417068"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6ceb8208c55ad8270e9b471d29abef7ac95b8d34de3f9bc83106ad8b8c4f8c50","event_uuid":"0f4e1f6f-f548-43c3-9f3f-e194eecb443c","position":{"commit_sha":"8e0c0245fc0b872a67fe4f9ecd6b9478afb8fcd1","position":"1785375590565609001-0f4e1f6f-f548-43c3-9f3f-e194eecb443c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"16d9afd91d020f485f33d749db47a64964d5f9ecee35f6d63453d0c7ce953243","event_uuid":"133c6b66-422a-47d2-b2cc-fb81f4c47336","position":{"commit_sha":"036d2b72da5b677138a3d3a471bc7c01c8df10e1","position":"1785375831188386041-133c6b66-422a-47d2-b2cc-fb81f4c47336"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"bdce800f-7053-4bf7-8ccb-afaa9acb1d55","comments":[],"created_at":1785371098181600001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c88bf3d7-d702-4bc9-9265-0a3bfcdaf84c","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"1803-df54-18bb-4881"},{"link_uuid":"98ec54af-4e51-4282-bde2-65d3034c33b3","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"jira-reb-1582"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`rebar link <a> <b> depends_on` can silently record a different edge than the one requested, and can produce an edge in which a ticket blocks its own subtree. Bug 1803-df54-18bb-4881 hit this while wiring epic 8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864's dependency graph: an epic ended up `depends_on` its own child, the requested child-level dependency was never recorded at all, and the operator had to retype children and hand-unlink the bad edge. Self-blocking edges distort `ready`, `next-batch` and the parent-first claim cascade, so parallel agents are handed a wrong work order.\n\nThe cause is a policy defect rather than a coding slip. `resolve_hierarchy_link` (`src/rebar/graph/_hierarchy.py:98`) decides \"comparable level\" for blocking links from the ticket's TYPE TIER (`_TYPE_TIER`, `src/rebar/graph/_hierarchy.py:26`) instead of from its position in the parent hierarchy. Bug jira-reb-1582 names the correct rule directly: comparability is structural, and any two tickets sharing a parent may hold a dependency. This story supersedes both bugs and replaces the policy.\n\n## Approach\n\nReplace type-tier comparability with structural (nearest-common-ancestor) comparability; add a resolved-pair invariant that makes ancestor-blocking edges unrepresentable regardless of how the edge was produced; then detect and repair the edges already written under the old rule.\n\nRejected alternative — keep the type tiers and special-case the failing shape by clamping promotion below the nearest common ancestor. That removes 1803's specific symptom but leaves comparability keyed on a ticket's *type*, so a task and a story that are genuine siblings still could not hold a direct dependency, and re-typing a ticket would silently rewrite the meaning of the dependency graph. jira-reb-1582 asks for the rule itself to change; patching the fallback at `src/rebar/graph/_hierarchy.py:93` would leave the store's semantics wrong in the same way.\n\nRejected alternative — reject cross-subtree blocking links with an error instead of escalating them. Honest, but it breaks every caller relying on auto-escalation today, including the `link` MCP tool and the reconciler's inbound apply path (`rebar.link` at `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py:502`). Escalation is retained, and its existing machine-readable redirect record (`src/rebar/graph/_links.py:207`) is kept as the loud signal.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- The blocking-link resolver decides comparability from the parent hierarchy alone; `_TYPE_TIER` no longer participates in that decision.\n- No blocking edge can exist between a ticket and its own ancestor or descendant, by any path into the resolver.\n- Blocking edges already written under the type-tier rule are detectable store-wide and repairable in a single pass.\n- The escalation contract callers depend on — auto-escalate a cross-subtree link, emit the redirect record — is unchanged.\n\n## Decomposition\n\nTwo children, in dependency order:\n\n1. **Structural comparability and the ancestor invariant** (leaf) — rewrites the resolver in `src/rebar/graph/_hierarchy.py` and moves the redundancy guard in `src/rebar/graph/_links.py` onto the resolved pair. This is the fix for both superseded bugs.\n2. **`link-audit` detection and repair** (leaf) — a store-wide scan plus one-shot repair for edges written under the old rule. It declares `depends_on` child 1, because the repair re-resolves each existing edge through the new resolver and cannot be written before those semantics are final.\n\nThe split follows the deliverable seam: child 1 changes what a new link means, child 2 fixes data already on disk. Each lands as one reviewable change. Neither is large enough to split further, and combining them would put a store-wide data rewrite in the same change as the semantics that rewrite depends on.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The repro from bug 1803-df54-18bb-4881 (a task and a story that are both direct children of one epic) records the requested task-to-story edge unchanged and produces no epic-to-child edge; verified by the regression test added in child 1, run against the store fixture.\n- [ ] The worked example from bug jira-reb-1582 resolves as that ticket specifies — Task D under Story C escalates to Story C when linked to Task B, while Task B to Story C records directly; verified by the regression test added in child 1.\n- [ ] `rebar link-audit` run twice against this repository's own tracker reports a non-empty first pass and an empty second pass after its repair; verified by running the command twice and comparing the two reports.\n- [ ] Both children are closed, each with its Gerrit change at `Verified +1` and `LLM-Review +1`; verified by the change status in Gerrit before each close.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `pytest tests/scripts/graph/` all pass; verified by running them in the worktree.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"Container story: every edit is delivered by its two children, which declare their own file impact.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"73caacc1-2e33-4032-ae07-af13b4417068","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"affe-2b42-4ee4-4e12","ticket_type":"story","title":"Resolve blocking-link comparability structurally, forbid ancestor self-blocks, and repair existing edges","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0380c875-2c65-4632-8903-e3bc98d0ac1a","c88bf3d7-d702-4bc9-9265-0a3bfcdaf84c","98ec54af-4e51-4282-bde2-65d3034c33b3","b776a60d-5ed1-4a4d-8f22-f4d35cd54469","593baf8c-1f3b-4ef1-b750-19709fea1429","109da523-0d5f-49cd-b252-93069bc2790c","73caacc1-2e33-4032-ae07-af13b4417068","0f4e1f6f-f548-43c3-9f3f-e194eecb443c","133c6b66-422a-47d2-b2cc-fb81f4c47336"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785375831188386042,"uuid":"e4fbd11c-4a14-4d1e-b2d4-6e3369732cfd"}